    {
      "id": "finance-ops-unvetted-accommodation",
      "question": "Can a traveller use an unvetted accommodation provider when Key Travel options do not meet their needs?",
      "answer_reference": "Yes, but only with the required insurance checks, risk assessment where applicable, and evidence satisfactory to the University contact.",
      "status": "answered",
      "answer": "Yes. Where accommodation available through Key Travel does not meet the traveller’s needs (for example locality or unreasonable cost) the traveller may source accommodation from an un‑vetted provider. The traveller must: 1) confirm the landlord has declared to their insurers that they rent out the property and is insured for fire, damage, loss etc.; 2) include lone‑traveller arrangements (e.g. renting spare rooms) in a travel risk assessment; 3) evidence these checks and any required risk assessment to the satisfaction of the University contact. On that basis bookings may be reclaimed via expenses. Note the policy advises travellers to seek Key Travel options first and discourages unregistered accommodation where possible.",
      "citation_ids": [
        "S1",
        "S2",
        "S3"
