      "id": "finance-ops-lost-original-receipt",
      "question": "What evidence may support an expense claim when the original receipt is unavailable?",
      "answer_reference": "Acceptable evidence can include an e-receipt, bank or credit-card statement, or a photograph, with an explanation for the missing original and evidence of payment.",
      "status": "answered",
      "answer": "If the original receipt is unavailable, acceptable supporting evidence includes: copies of e-receipts, bank statements and/or credit card statements, or a photograph/scan of the receipt, together with a justification for absence of the original. For foreign-currency transactions, proof of conversion (e.g. credit card statement) may be required. Where receipts cannot be obtained for subsistence or incidental expenses, the claimant must include dates/times and details of actual expenditure and may claim up to the published thresholds (and for incidental items up to the stated daily limits).",
